prefs-proton-lead = Proton runs Somnium (a Windows game) on Linux. Pick the build Somnium uses: Unilux downloads it, then adds the Wine patches Somnium needs (see Wine patches). "patches verified" builds work right away; the others need podman or docker to build those patches first, which takes a while.
prefs-patches-lead = Stock Proton lacks a few fixes Somnium needs: TLS client certificates for sign-in, and video playback. Unilux ships them as a bundle of Wine DLLs copied over the Proton in use. Nothing to do here normally; the Proton page handles it. Use this page to check the files, rebuild them or undo them.
prefs-patches-current = Bundle on the current Proton
prefs-patches-build-missing = Needs podman or docker, neither is installed. Install podman, then reopen this page.
prefs-patches-build-optional = Not needed: a verified bundle already fits this Proton. Rebuild only if it misbehaves; Wine compiles in podman (long), then the result replaces it.
prefs-patches-build-missing-cmd = Needs podman or docker, neither is installed. Install podman, then reopen this page:
prefs-patches-files = Patch sources
prefs-patches-build = Build a bundle for the current Proton
prefs-patches-build-sub = No published bundle fits this Proton: compiles Wine with the patches in podman or docker, then applies them. Takes a while; follow it in Logs.
prefs-patches-restore = Remove the patches (restore stock files)
